+# opencode / agent notes
+
+- `rtk` proxy output can be empty/unreliable for `ls`, `du`, glob listings. When you need full tool output, either:
+  - use `rtk proxy`, or
+  - ignore the rtk directive and run the plain command (e.g. `/bin/ls`, `find`, `du`) directly.
+- Do not trust `rtk ls`/`rtk read` empty results as proof a path is empty/missing; use `find`/`/bin/ls`/read as cross-check.
+- Pristine test environments: `git archive HEAD | tar -x -C /tmp/<dir>` + `npm ci` gives a clean tree matching CI; the main workspace `node_modules` contains leftover extraneous packages (knip, oxc-*) and tracked derived state, so it is NOT faithful for verification.
